WEBVTT

00:00:02.750 --> 00:00:03.881
Whoo! That's better.

00:00:04.016 --> 00:00:05.981
Now I finally have some energy!

00:00:06.116 --> 00:00:07.523
Did you just braid my hair?

00:00:07.659 --> 00:00:08.985
You're welcome.
It looks so good.

00:00:09.120 --> 00:00:10.654
- I love it!
- SPRUCE: Wow.

00:00:10.790 --> 00:00:12.090
These fries are amazing.

00:00:12.225 --> 00:00:13.957
They'd really go great
with a burger.

00:00:14.092 --> 00:00:16.061
- (screaming)
- (others gasping)

00:00:17.367 --> 00:00:19.329
What is happening?

00:00:19.464 --> 00:00:21.367
Yeah, we try not to use
that word around here.

00:00:21.503 --> 00:00:24.032
It's just that "burger" sounds
a little too much like, uh...

00:00:24.168 --> 00:00:25.440
(whispers):
"Bergens."

00:00:25.575 --> 00:00:26.740
(Putt Putt trolls screaming)

00:00:26.876 --> 00:00:30.574
- We call burgers...
- ♪ ♪

00:00:30.710 --> 00:00:32.208
meat circles.

00:00:32.344 --> 00:00:33.913
- Clay?
- Clay. Hey, what's up, man?

00:00:34.048 --> 00:00:36.282
(laughing):
Hey. How you been, man?

00:00:36.417 --> 00:00:37.350
Clay!

00:00:37.485 --> 00:00:38.482
Hmm. John.

00:00:38.617 --> 00:00:39.519
Wha...

00:00:39.654 --> 00:00:41.885
Spruce. What do you know?

00:00:42.020 --> 00:00:43.722
Actually, I go by Bruce now.

00:00:43.858 --> 00:00:46.328
Bruce. Oh, someone got fancy.

00:00:46.464 --> 00:00:47.830
- I like it.
- (laughs)

00:00:47.965 --> 00:00:50.127
Look who's talking.
Is that a sweater romper?

00:00:50.262 --> 00:00:52.202
What can I say?
When you co-run a place,

00:00:52.337 --> 00:00:53.395
got to flex the drip.

00:00:53.530 --> 00:00:55.067
Yeah, I'm the fun side
of the operation,

00:00:55.203 --> 00:00:56.802
and Mr. Clay takes care
of the boring stuff.

00:00:56.937 --> 00:00:58.267
- Guilty. (chuckles)
- (laughs)

00:00:58.403 --> 00:01:00.809
- Whoa! Baby Branch?
- (Branch chuckles)

00:01:00.944 --> 00:01:02.643
- No way.
- Actually, it's Big Branch now.

00:01:02.778 --> 00:01:04.612
- (Clay gasps)
- Or just Branch.

00:01:04.747 --> 00:01:06.078
- Branch is fine.
- Come here.

00:01:06.213 --> 00:01:08.045
- Come here. Aw, yeah.
- (chuckles): Yeah.

00:01:08.181 --> 00:01:10.312
- So, Clay, this is Poppy.
- Hi, Clay.

00:01:10.447 --> 00:01:12.119
- So great to finally meet you.
- Whoa!

00:01:12.254 --> 00:01:14.452
Can you do the Rusty Robot
for me? (snorting chuckle)

00:01:14.587 --> 00:01:15.887
Yeah, no.

00:01:16.022 --> 00:01:17.419
I don't do that anymore, okay?

00:01:17.555 --> 00:01:19.189
Right. Kidding.
(chuckles) Can you imagine?

00:01:19.325 --> 00:01:20.925
I wouldn't just
ask you to do that

00:01:21.060 --> 00:01:22.759
after meeting you
two seconds ago.

00:01:22.894 --> 00:01:24.295
Who would do that?

00:01:24.430 --> 00:01:26.033
Yeah, it's just that
Fun Boy Clay is dead.

00:01:26.168 --> 00:01:29.601
Serious Boy Clay only does
the Well-Oiled Robot,

00:01:29.736 --> 00:01:31.168
and it is no...

00:01:31.303 --> 00:01:33.102
(imitates record scratching)
...fun.

00:01:33.237 --> 00:01:34.840
I mean, that's still pretty fun.

00:01:34.975 --> 00:01:36.840
(chuckles) Yeah, same old Clay.

00:01:36.976 --> 00:01:38.242
No, that's not true.

00:01:38.377 --> 00:01:40.781
If I was still fun,
would I have chosen

00:01:40.917 --> 00:01:43.482
the admin building
as my bedroom?

00:01:43.617 --> 00:01:45.648
(bird caws)

00:01:45.783 --> 00:01:46.952
Huh? Huh?

00:01:47.088 --> 00:01:49.253
Asking the tough questions, guys.

00:01:49.388 --> 00:01:51.893
- Asking the tough questions.
- Oh, right.

00:01:52.028 --> 00:01:54.363
Anyway, I can't believe
you all are here.

00:01:54.499 --> 00:01:55.795
Wait, where's Floyd?

00:01:55.930 --> 00:01:57.261
That's why we're here.

00:01:57.397 --> 00:01:58.999
Floyd's been taken prisoner
in Mount Rageous

00:01:59.134 --> 00:02:01.003
by superstar singers
Velvet and Veneer...

00:02:01.139 --> 00:02:03.439
ALL: ...and the only thing
powerful enough to free him

00:02:03.575 --> 00:02:05.070
is the perfect family harmony.

00:02:05.205 --> 00:02:07.874
Okay, either they just
made that up,

00:02:08.010 --> 00:02:10.210
or I have not been
paying attention.

00:02:10.346 --> 00:02:12.107
Well, why haven't you just
called the authorities?

00:02:12.243 --> 00:02:14.749
Oh, unless Floyd is being held

00:02:14.885 --> 00:02:17.153
in an impenetrable
diamond prison.

00:02:17.288 --> 00:02:18.447
Yeah, that.

00:02:18.582 --> 00:02:20.286
I'm in.
I'd also like to volunteer

00:02:20.422 --> 00:02:22.959
to keep track of our expenses,
just 'cause I think

00:02:23.094 --> 00:02:24.886
you're gonna need somebody
to be on top of that.

00:02:25.022 --> 00:02:27.624
Yeah, I don't think you'll get
any pushback on that front.

00:02:27.759 --> 00:02:31.165
Great, but we need to leave
for Mount Rageous, like, now.

00:02:31.300 --> 00:02:33.196
You can't leave now.
You just got here. Come on.

00:02:33.332 --> 00:02:35.335
- Let me show you around.
- (Poppy yelps)

00:02:35.470 --> 00:02:36.438
Hug time!

00:02:36.574 --> 00:02:37.601
- (chuckles)
- Uh...

00:02:37.736 --> 00:02:38.735
Yeah, no.

00:02:38.870 --> 00:02:40.205
Aw, so cute.

00:02:40.341 --> 00:02:42.070
Where'd you get
that hug time bracelet?

00:02:42.205 --> 00:02:43.611
My dad gave it to me.

00:02:43.746 --> 00:02:46.177
Okay, this is so totally random,

00:02:46.312 --> 00:02:48.515
but I used to have one
just like it.

00:02:48.650 --> 00:02:50.046
Can I see that?

00:02:50.181 --> 00:02:52.154
Wow. It fits you perfectly.

00:02:52.289 --> 00:02:53.350
Yeah.

00:02:59.461 --> 00:03:01.397
Whoa.

00:03:01.533 --> 00:03:02.962
(chuckles) I'm sorry.

00:03:03.098 --> 00:03:05.399
What did you say
your name was again?

00:03:05.535 --> 00:03:06.935
I'm Poppy.

00:03:07.832 --> 00:03:09.069
Poppy?

00:03:20.084 --> 00:03:22.716
Okay, um, another
totally random, weird question,

00:03:22.851 --> 00:03:26.790
but is your dad King Peppy?

00:03:27.624 --> 00:03:29.457
Uh, yeah. (chuckles)

00:03:29.592 --> 00:03:31.021
You're... (gasps)

00:03:31.157 --> 00:03:32.488
You're-you're alive!

00:03:32.624 --> 00:03:34.830
- I'm alive.
- VIVA: This is unbelievable!

00:03:34.966 --> 00:03:36.997
I never thought
I'd see you again.

00:03:37.132 --> 00:03:39.795
- Again?
- Poppy, it's me, Viva.

00:03:39.930 --> 00:03:40.897
Uh...

00:03:41.032 --> 00:03:42.634
I'm your sister.

00:03:42.770 --> 00:03:44.572
My... my what?

00:03:44.708 --> 00:03:46.642
Your sister. Your hermana.

00:03:46.777 --> 00:03:48.075
- Whoa.
- TINY DIAMOND: Hey, man.

00:03:48.210 --> 00:03:50.646
Am I the only one
without a long-lost sibling?

00:03:50.782 --> 00:03:52.011
What do you mean we're sisters?

00:03:52.147 --> 00:03:53.676
H-How could I have not
known about you?

00:03:53.812 --> 00:03:55.717
I can't believe Dad didn't
tell me I have a sister.

00:03:55.852 --> 00:03:57.481
- That is so Dad. (laughs)
- So Dad.

00:03:57.616 --> 00:03:59.119
Aah! I can't...
I can't believe this.

00:03:59.254 --> 00:04:00.782
I've always dreamt
of having a sister.

00:04:00.918 --> 00:04:02.686
I was just saying this.
Wasn't I just saying this?

00:04:02.821 --> 00:04:04.188
This means we can plan
each other's birthday parties.

00:04:04.324 --> 00:04:05.653
- Yeah, yeah, yeah, and weddings.
- Yes!

00:04:05.789 --> 00:04:07.692
My best friend Bridget
just had her wedding,

00:04:07.828 --> 00:04:09.460
and it went off without a hitch
'cause I was, like, the best

00:04:09.596 --> 00:04:11.231
maid of honor. -You'd be
the best maid of honor.

00:04:11.367 --> 00:04:13.102
(gasps) You and Bridget
are gonna love each other!

00:04:13.238 --> 00:04:14.263
Oh, my gosh. I'm gonna love her.
I love what you love.

00:04:14.398 --> 00:04:15.404
- Yes! (exclaims)
- (laughing): Yes!

00:04:15.540 --> 00:04:16.831
♪ Kaleidoscopic ♪

00:04:16.967 --> 00:04:20.237
♪ I'm seeing different
when I look at you ♪

00:04:20.373 --> 00:04:22.877
♪ Everything's looking bright ♪

00:04:23.012 --> 00:04:24.575
♪ No, I can't stop it now ♪

00:04:24.711 --> 00:04:28.717
♪ I'm getting swept up
in a feel-good mood ♪

00:04:28.852 --> 00:04:30.984
♪ Feeling I can't deny ♪

00:04:31.119 --> 00:04:32.588
♪ Now that you're with me ♪

00:04:32.723 --> 00:04:34.286
♪ I can finally see ♪

00:04:34.421 --> 00:04:36.825
♪ Colors that were
up in my mind ♪

00:04:36.960 --> 00:04:38.859
♪ Didn't know I was blind ♪

00:04:38.994 --> 00:04:40.355
♪ Now that I'm with you ♪

00:04:40.490 --> 00:04:41.961
♪ Sparks are flying loose ♪

00:04:42.096 --> 00:04:44.800
♪ Fireworks go off in my brain ♪

00:04:44.936 --> 00:04:47.167
♪ And I'll never be the same ♪

00:04:47.303 --> 00:04:49.969
♪ I didn't know
until I found you ♪

00:04:50.104 --> 00:04:52.304
♪ Having the time of our lives ♪

00:04:52.439 --> 00:04:55.175
- ♪ It takes two ♪
- ♪ It takes two ♪

00:04:55.310 --> 00:04:58.014
♪ When I look up,
the stars are brighter ♪

00:04:58.149 --> 00:05:01.347
♪ Now I know everything's
better with you ♪

00:05:01.482 --> 00:05:03.947
- ♪ It takes two ♪
- ♪ Ooh, ooh, ooh ♪

00:05:04.083 --> 00:05:05.383
♪ Now, now that ♪

00:05:05.518 --> 00:05:08.086
♪ Now that we got it
all together ♪

00:05:08.221 --> 00:05:09.518
♪ Now we're together ♪

00:05:09.654 --> 00:05:11.287
- ♪ We got it all ♪
- ♪ Hey! ♪

00:05:11.422 --> 00:05:12.896
- ♪ Now ♪
- ♪ Now ♪

00:05:13.031 --> 00:05:14.326
- ♪ Now that ♪
- ♪ Now that ♪

00:05:14.461 --> 00:05:16.032
♪ Now that we got it
all together ♪

00:05:16.167 --> 00:05:17.763
- ♪ Hey! ♪
- ♪ Now we're together ♪

00:05:17.899 --> 00:05:19.432
♪ We got it all ♪

00:05:19.568 --> 00:05:21.169
♪ You've got me feeling right,
feeling right ♪

00:05:21.304 --> 00:05:23.400
♪ Feeling like
good vibes are at my door ♪

00:05:23.536 --> 00:05:26.035
♪ Every day, every night,
ooh, ooh ♪

00:05:26.170 --> 00:05:27.735
♪ It takes two ♪

00:05:27.871 --> 00:05:30.713
♪ I didn't know
until I found you ♪

00:05:30.848 --> 00:05:33.048
♪ Having the time of our lives ♪

00:05:33.183 --> 00:05:35.144
- ♪ It takes two ♪
- ♪ It takes two ♪

00:05:35.279 --> 00:05:39.686
♪ It takes me ♪

00:05:39.821 --> 00:05:41.150
♪ And you. ♪

00:05:41.285 --> 00:05:42.552
(Poppy and Viva laughing)

00:05:42.687 --> 00:05:44.457
So, I was thinking about
getting more into, like,

00:05:44.592 --> 00:05:46.994
reading short stories and essays
instead of full novels.

00:05:47.130 --> 00:05:49.593
- Ooh, I love that for you.
- Yeah.

00:05:49.728 --> 00:05:51.727
But, um... but just to
circle back real quick.

00:05:51.862 --> 00:05:55.134
I still have a million questions
about what happened.

00:05:55.270 --> 00:05:56.299
I used to live
at the Troll Tree.

00:05:56.434 --> 00:05:57.765
I was there when you were born.

00:05:57.901 --> 00:05:59.501
And you were so cute,
kind of like you are now,

00:05:59.637 --> 00:06:01.541
only teensier
and weensier and...

00:06:01.677 --> 00:06:04.075
Oh. Do you want to make candy
necklaces that we never finish

00:06:04.211 --> 00:06:05.810
because we eat all the candy?

00:06:05.945 --> 00:06:07.180
Obviously!

00:06:07.316 --> 00:06:09.150
But, Veev,
I'm just gonna need you

00:06:09.285 --> 00:06:11.547
to focus here
and-and tell me everything.

00:06:11.682 --> 00:06:13.752
Why am I only learning
about you now?

00:06:13.888 --> 00:06:15.189
What happened?

00:06:15.324 --> 00:06:17.391
(robotic voice):
We got accidentally separated.

00:06:17.526 --> 00:06:19.426
(normal voice):
And I've lived here ever since.

00:06:19.562 --> 00:06:20.630
The end.

00:06:20.765 --> 00:06:21.928
Want to do candy toe rings next?

00:06:22.063 --> 00:06:24.296
Uh, accidentally separated?

00:06:24.431 --> 00:06:26.235
Viva doesn't like
to talk about it--

00:06:26.371 --> 00:06:28.335
it's too painful for her--
but she's been here

00:06:28.470 --> 00:06:30.637
ever since the night
of the great Bergen attack.

00:06:30.773 --> 00:06:32.007
(Viva humming)

00:06:32.143 --> 00:06:33.336
Viva, are you talking
about the night

00:06:33.471 --> 00:06:35.740
the trolls escaped Bergen Town?

00:06:35.875 --> 00:06:37.141
Oh. Yeah.

00:06:37.276 --> 00:06:39.107
Yeah, I guess it was that night.

00:06:39.243 --> 00:06:41.015
(resumes humming)

00:06:41.151 --> 00:06:43.512
Not everyone made it out
of that tree.

00:06:43.648 --> 00:06:45.382
Some of them got trapped
by Bergens.

00:06:45.518 --> 00:06:47.256
They were this close
to getting eaten,

00:06:47.392 --> 00:06:49.421
until Viva and some of the
other trolls fought them off.

00:06:49.556 --> 00:06:51.825
- (Viva grunting fiercely)
- (Bergens screaming)

00:06:51.961 --> 00:06:53.761
CLAY:
But by then,

00:06:53.897 --> 00:06:55.195
the tunnels had collapsed,

00:06:55.330 --> 00:06:57.131
and they were cut off
from the rest.

00:06:57.267 --> 00:06:59.828
I kept screaming,
"No troll left behind!"

00:06:59.963 --> 00:07:03.436
But when I went back in,
the tunnels had collapsed.

00:07:03.572 --> 00:07:06.505
That's when I found
Viva's hug time bracelet.

00:07:06.640 --> 00:07:09.540
Viva found this old,
abandoned Bergen golf course

00:07:09.675 --> 00:07:11.708
and transformed it
into this troll utopia.

00:07:11.843 --> 00:07:14.678
We formed this little sanctuary
of survivors.

00:07:14.814 --> 00:07:17.450
I added fire exits.
She added her heart and soul.

00:07:17.586 --> 00:07:19.651
I've thought so many times
about leaving, you know,

00:07:19.787 --> 00:07:24.260
to look for you and Dad,
but it's not safe out there.

00:07:24.396 --> 00:07:28.829
I know I should've told Poppy,
but my heart was broken.

00:07:28.964 --> 00:07:30.295
I felt like a failure,

00:07:30.430 --> 00:07:33.194
not just as a king
but as a father.

00:07:33.330 --> 00:07:34.770
I feel so guilty.

00:07:34.906 --> 00:07:36.204
What do you think I should do?

00:07:36.339 --> 00:07:39.173
I'm afraid that's
our time for today.

00:07:39.308 --> 00:07:42.045
But I just revealed
a major trauma.

